fore delivering a recommendation that cites exact CV wording, verify each citation:\n\n```bash\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/evidence_check.py claims.json\n```\n\n`claims.json` is a JSON array: `[{\"file\": \"cv.pdf\", \"page\": 2, \"quote\": \"exact text from that CV\"}]`. Quotes are whitespace-normalized, so line breaks inside a PDF quote are fine. The checker fails (exit 2) on: quote absent, quote on a different page than claimed, out-of-range page, or any file-level extraction error — and reports the page(s) where the quote actually is. Fix the report before delivering.\n\n## Step 4 — Deliver task-sized output\n\n- Default deliverable: a short recommendation with per-requirement evidence (quote + page) and a clear verdict. Surface hard risks prominently (e.g. salary/location mismatch, missing mandatory evidence) as items to verify before or during interview.\n- Full evaluation report only on request. No all-requirement ledger, no forced long format, no extra deliverables the user did not ask for.\n- Match the user's language; keep their addressing preferences.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Explicit file errors are reported as failures, never laundered into success.\n- Extraction/quote validation is mechanical; qualification interpretation stays semantic and human-reviewable.\n- No protected-attribute-based filtering; no invented experience.\n"}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1793079034346, "__openclaw": {"runId": "2e88e318-1555-4361-875c-567dc5c6690b"}}}
